Description: Change Sun RPC code licence to BSD-3-Clause
 Replace the non-free Sun RPC licence notice in print-sunrpc.c, rpc_auth.h
 and rpc_msg.h with the BSD-3-Clause notice under which Sun Microsystems,
 Inc. relicensed the Sun RPC code. This reproduces the change made in the
 FreeBSD source tree in 2013, see
 https://cgit.freebsd.org/src/commit/?id=2e322d379631c3bd6107e295f3e5d814c7845fc7
 .
 Backported from upstream; the hunk for the upstream CHANGES file was
 dropped because it does not apply to the 4.99 branch.
Author: Denis Ovsienko <denis@ovsienko.info>
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/the-tcpdump-group/tcpdump/commit/b4c1686936096a305faadc866333c11b81e3c2f9
Bug: https://github.com/the-tcpdump-group/tcpdump/issues/1167
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/1147928
Last-Update: 2026-11-02
---
 print-sunrpc.c | 51 +++++++++++++++++++++++++--------------------------
 rpc_auth.h     | 47 +++++++++++++++++++++++------------------------
 rpc_msg.h      | 47 +++++++++++++++++++++++------------------------
 3 files changed, 71 insertions(+), 74 deletions(-)

